{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# s3 doctor should fold bundle heads into the published ref, not the worktree HEAD\n\n## Context\n\nSplit out of bug `gnarled-acardiac-bettong` (landed as Gerrit 1628), which proved the defect and\nclosed the silent-corruption door with a loud refusal. This ticket is the proper fix that\nrefusal stands in for, and retires the refusal.\n\nToday `_fold_heads` (`src/rebar/_store/s3_doctor.py:232-261`) merges every fetched bundle head\ninto the tracker WORKTREE's HEAD with `git merge` and returns `git rev-parse HEAD`. Because\n`git merge` only merges into the checked-out branch, the heal's result is a function of whatever\nbranch the tracker happens to be on. `_require_tracker_on_ref` (`s3_doctor.py:167-195`) therefore\nrefuses the heal outright whenever `current_branch != ref` (detached HEAD included), so the\ndoctor is SAFE but cannot heal such a tracker at all.\n\n## Premise validated against origin/main (cc69cc1179)\n\n- The guard and its \"retires with envious-metal-budgie\" docstring are present at\n  `s3_doctor.py:167-195`; `_heal_locked` calls it at `s3_doctor.py:136`.\n- `_publish_and_prune` (`s3_doctor.py:264-317`) now relies on that guard: its docstring records\n  that the `git branch -f` fallback was removed, and it bundles `HEAD` + `refs/heads/<ref>` at\n  `s3_doctor.py:285`.\n- Regression floor is GREEN today: `tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py` +\n  `test_s3_doctor_heldout.py` = 18 passed, 1 skipped.\n\n## Mechanism decision (experimentally settled, not assumed)\n\nThe ticket left the mechanism open (`merge-tree`/`commit-tree` vs a scratch worktree). Probed\nboth concerns on Git 2.55 in a throwaway repo shaped like the tracker:\n\n- `git merge-tree --write-tree A B` DOES honour the tracker's configured `ours` driver\n  (`merge.ours.driver=true`, set by `src/rebar/_commands/init.py:559`) together with the\n  tickets-branch `.gitattributes` `.bridge_state/* merge=ours` line\n  (`_commands/init.py:62`). It produced a tree byte-identical to the worktree `git merge` on the\n  same inputs, and it CONFLICTS identically when the driver is absent. So the merge policy AC is\n  satisfiable without a worktree.\n- A real content conflict exits non-zero and names the conflicted paths — and, unlike `git\n  merge`, leaves NO worktree/index state, so no `merge --abort` is needed.\n- `git commit-tree <tree> -p <ref-tip> -p <head>` builds the 2-parent merge commit; unrelated\n  histories need `--allow-unrelated-histories` on `merge-tree`.\n\nA scratch worktree was rejected: it costs a full checkout of the event tree on every heal.\n`merge-tree` needs no checkout and never touches the worktree. Git floor is already 2.38 for\n`merge-tree --write-tree` (README.md:143-147, `tests/unit/test_git_version_floor.py`).\n\n## Plan\n\n1. **Rewrite `_fold_heads` (`s3_doctor.py:232-261`)** to fold into the published ref, not HEAD:\n   start from `refs/heads/<ref>`'s tip; for each head ref, skip if already an ancestor of the\n   running tip; else `git merge-tree --write-tree [--allow-unrelated-histories] <tip> <head>`\n   then `git commit-tree <tree> -p <tip> -p <head> -m \"Merge <head> (s3 doctor auto-heal of ref\n   <ref>)\"`. A non-zero `merge-tree` still raises `S3DoctorConflict` with the same message shape\n   (the existing hint carrying `fsck-recover` is preserved). Keep the existing write lock and the\n   iterated 2-parent shape. Where `--allow-unrelated-histories` is unavailable (Git < 2.41), fail\n   as a loud `S3DoctorConflict` naming the Git version, never a silent skip.\n2. **Move the ref (`_heal_locked`, `s3_doctor.py:136-143`)**: publish the folded sha onto\n   `refs/heads/<ref>` under the same lock. When `ref` is NOT checked out:\n   `git update-ref refs/heads/<ref> <merged> <old-tip>` — a compare-and-swap, so a concurrent\n   mover aborts the heal instead of clobbering. When `ref` IS the checked-out branch: `git reset\n   --hard <merged>`, so index and worktree stay consistent with the branch exactly as the old\n   `git merge` left them.\n3. **Replace the refusal guard**: delete `_require_tracker_on_ref` (`s3_doctor.py:167-195`) and\n   its call (`s3_doctor.py:136`). In its place, a much narrower pre-download guard: when `ref` IS\n   checked out and the worktree is dirty, refuse before downloading anything (today's `git merge`\n   already fails on a dirty worktree, later and less clearly — this keeps that refusal and makes\n   it early). A tracker on another branch or detached HEAD is no longer refused at all.\n4. **Fix `_publish_and_prune` (`s3_doctor.py:264-317`)**: its docstring's \"guard has established\n   ref IS the checked-out branch\" reasoning is retired. Bundle `refs/heads/<ref>` explicitly\n   rather than relying on `HEAD` agreeing (`s3_doctor.py:285`); off-branch, HEAD no longer names\n   the merged tip.\n5. **Tests** (`tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py`): convert the three refusal tests\n   (`:206`, `:235`, `:251`) into HEAL tests — a side-branch tracker and a detached-HEAD tracker\n   both heal losslessly, and no commit reachable only from the side branch becomes reachable from\n   the published ref. Keep `:275` (single-bundle no-op off the ref). Add: the side branch and the\n   worktree HEAD are UNMOVED by an off-branch heal; the dirty-worktree refusal; and an\n   on-branch heal still advances HEAD/index/worktree. `merge=ours` and real-conflict coverage\n   already exist in `test_s3_doctor_heldout.py:81,109` and must stay green unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The heal folds heads into the published ref's tip regardless of the tracker's checked-out\n      branch.\n- [ ] No commit reachable only from the checked-out branch becomes reachable from the published\n      ref.\n- [ ] The existing merge policy is preserved: `.bridge_state/* merge=ours` still applies and a\n      real conflict still aborts and raises rather than resolving silently.\n- [ ] A tracker on a different branch, and a detached-HEAD tracker, both heal successfully —\n      replacing the refusal that `gnarled-acardiac-bettong` installed.\n- [ ] The refusal guard from `gnarled-acardiac-bettong` is removed, and off-branch/detached heals\n      are proven by tests that fail before this change.\n- [ ] An on-branch heal leaves index and worktree consistent with the moved ref (no phantom\n      deletions in `git status`); an off-branch heal leaves the checked-out branch and worktree\n      untouched.\n- [ ] The 18 existing s3_doctor tests stay green; `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786558301245755001,"uuid":"044e63fb-83be-4790-b5f5-9164ca3e2dc4"}